{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt","id":1449302,"title":"Tremere Pyramid Rebuilt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-22T19:08:27-07:00","id":1449302,"title":"Tremere Pyramid Rebuilt","content":"So. Tremere can not blood bond other vampires. But can they participate in the vaulderie? If they can I think we can rebuild the pyramid. Correct me if I'm wrong. The council has a vinculum with each other, then each council member has one with all of their pontifex (either individually or as a group). Then each pontifex has one with all of their lords (either individually or as a group). Then each lord has one with all of their regents (either individually or as a group). Then each regent has one with their apprentices.<br /> <br /> My vote would be to do these individually as to keep a greater level of inner clan rivalry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T23:20:52-07:00","id":1449325,"title":"","content":"1. I do not think they have stated anywhere that the vaulderie would still work for them.<br /> 2. It would most likely trigger the traitor mark - might be awkward.<br /> 3. I would absolutely expect them to specifically say it does not work in a future book, if this idea becomes popular. They are supposed to be <b>The Broken Clan</b> for some reason.<br /> <br /> In game it might be a work around. I would allow it (if you add in at least one non clan members blood for it to work. The vaulderie magic needs it for some reason. To add some draw back)<br /> <br /> From the bit of information we have I am not positive the different factions would let themselves be bound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26030,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","user":"mfalkenb","date":". 05-23-2021, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T23:35:08-07:00","id":1449326,"title":"","content":"Oh the poor Tremere. One of the original clans from 1st edition but for some reason the writers could never stop messing with the clan, its back story, or stop adding twists.<br /> <br /> Half the backstory and design of the clan suggests rigid order and near perfect lockstep between all members, the other half says it is the exact opposite. In other words the clan was less designed and more of a plot device that changed attributes based on what the writers needed to make their stories work.<br /> <br /> Rebuilding the pyramid doesn't require anything beyond simply abandoning all the contrary materials added for non-sensical reasons. The partial blood bonding to the council, the clan discipline of dominate, and the fact that the Tremere are hyper selective about who gets embraced means the Tremere is a small clan, made of like minded individuals, whose shared interests and need for mutual defense ensures that they have to stick together to survive.<br /> <br /> Once you have that as the bedrock, you just expand the frame work while maintaining the standards.<br /> <br /> If anything in my opinion, starting from a point of promoting inner clan rivalry for the Tremere sounds a lot like suggesting all Brujah would agree to rebelling in the same way, it more or less misses the point of the clan. If I was going to be uncharitable it sounds a lot like turning the Tremere into Hogwarts with its house system.<br /> <br /> The Tremere stole the power of vampirism for themselves, they as a clan are battle hardened by being attacked for centuries by some of the more powerful clans (as in not even Vozhd can crack a chantry defense), and despite having minimal numbers they not only held their ground, they thrived enough to become a valued part of the Camarilla. Not even the Giovanni can lay claim to that level of systemic lockstep and they are blood related in two different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T02:33:35-07:00","id":1449331,"title":"","content":"IIRC in V5 there isn't a &quot;Transubstantiation of Seven&quot; ritual translation yet for the Tremere, and with the Council gone I'd doubt that'll be coming back. Individual Houses might adapt it to something not so complex as how the Council orchestrated the initiation of the neonates worldwide with this ritual, but it might bring ideas on how to mystically bind their subjects with blood magic.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T11:15:41-07:00","id":1449362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1449331#post1449331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC in V5 there isn't a &quot;Transubstantiation of Seven&quot; ritual translation yet for the Tremere</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there one written out for V20?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T12:16:36-07:00","id":1449478,"title":"","content":"Tremere are a clan where at first you look at them and think &quot;hold on a minute, these fellows seem like OP mary sues and for some reason all the dork powergamers with no social skills want to pick them, I hate them, they need a nerf&quot; and then when you learn a little more you realise that their backstory makes complete sense, that their power is justified, and that dork powergamers will be dork powergamers with whatever clan they like and the Tremere are a clan of choice because they provide options rather than an issue with balancing, and also they're infamously not that charismatic so it's ok to play a dork Tremre...&quot; <br /> <br /> A good chunk of writers get stuck with their initial assumption and don't look further than that. It's was a problem that began long before V5, and these ill-advised revisions for the clan became the stepping stone for the farce the Tremere are put in for V5. The V5 move is also motivated by this strange idea that clans should be more inclusive for different types of people, which is... exactly the opposite of what clans and sects are all about. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, it boils down as follows: <br /> The Tremere benefit immensely from their clan structure. A Tremere not in the pyramid is not going to be successful, because only 2/3 disciplines will work without either tutelage or more studying than a hungry lone neonate can really commit to. If they are a thaumaturgical talent, they may be press-ganged into serving some local lord or otherwise become an unwelcome competitor that drives prices down. The pyramid provides resources, security, and brand recognition. <br /> <br /> The Tremere are going to embrace likeminded people, and their vetting process is going to be heavy, because if you're going to share a communal haven with undying folk you're going to pick folks you can all stand, or at least not cause problems, You also want people who're going to be on a similar page to teach magic too, because ideas communicate better when you're all keeping within the same framework. <br /> <br /> What kind of Tremere would join house Carna? None of them. That's not who Tremere are. The paradigm is wrong, and if it was a real competitor you'd be killed for joining. HC might maybe work if you fled for the hills and embraced some fledglings just to fill a chantry, but that kind of approach will bite you in the ass. You can only reasonably conclude that the Tremere split is either A: Pure silly/wish fulfilment or B: A trojan horse designed to get Tremere into territories that hate Tremere, and perhaps an attempt to make the Tremere look less threatening so that the Ventrue don't curb their ambitions. <br /> <br /> So, using reason, you can only either Ignore the split or run with the idea that it's just a ruse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T12:28:17-07:00","id":1449480,"title":"","content":"I always thought Tremere were a little overrated in older editions, because they didn't have Celerity, which was the big combat discipline in older editions, and they didn't have the social skills or time to spend socializing needed to get lots of political power and canon-fodder. A Tremere that pisses off a Brujah is going to have his fireball dodged and then be torn limb from limb in the blink of an eye, if it's a direct confrontation. In an indirect confrontation, the Brujah will use it's control over the Unions to have the Tremere's haven bulldozed in broad daylight.<br /> <br /> Anyway, White Wolf knows what side its toast is buttered on, so it is angling to appeal more to the Wiccans who work at Hot Topic than to the Harry Potter fans, which is probably a smart financial play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T13:31:54-07:00","id":1449484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1449480#post1449480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought Tremere were a little overrated in older editions, because they didn't have Celerity, which was the big combat discipline in older editions, and they didn't have the social skills or time to spend socializing needed to get lots of political power and canon-fodder. A Tremere that pisses off a Brujah is going to have his fireball dodged and then be torn limb from limb in the blink of an eye, if it's a direct confrontation. In an indirect confrontation, the Brujah will use it's control over the Unions to have the Tremere's haven bulldozed in broad daylight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually your issue with the brujah vs. tremere shows exactly what the semi-truck sized plot hole with the Tremere is. Namely what are they when not casting spells. Through out the editions the writers never really explained how the clan paid its bills or maintained influence.<br /> <br /> The best they came up with was the Tremere would trade their spell use for boons so that the local Primogen owed the local Tremere a favor, so when said Brujah got annoying the Tremere would use the Primogen as his fireball. Essentially the Tremere were supposed to fight more like Little Finger than Daenerys Targaryen, but the writers never got around to it, so they just used the full package design with Tremere 2.0 a.k.a. the Giovanni, another insular clan with a strict hierarchy, active 3rd generation leader, access to clan specific magic, has dominate as a clan discipline, and is generally hated by most if not all. The main difference is that the Giovanni are also bankers and have potence intead of auspex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T17:48:45-07:00","id":1449496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1449484#post1449484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually your issue with the brujah vs. tremere shows exactly what the semi-truck sized plot hole with the Tremere is. Namely what are they when not casting spells. Through out the editions the writers never really explained how the clan paid its bills or maintained influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always imagined that the Regent of the local chantry decided what the local priorities of the chantry were, influenced by instruction he received upstairs from the lord (who in turn got some instructions from the Pontifex). So if one Regent only wanted to do mystical research and nothing else, that's what that chantry did absent some minimal maintenance work like making sure they built enough Influence or Resources by using Dominate, the Blood Bond, or simply their investment portfolio to pay taxes and utilities for the chantry. If another Regent in the city next door wanted to grow Influence in the mortal realm and treat the Chantry like a masonic fraternal organization, then that's what they did. If a third Regent had a very specific goal in mind like deciding who will be the next Prince, quelling the local Anarchs who tagged one of the chantries with spraypaint, or bending the domain's Primogen Council to his will, then they worked on that.<br /> <br /> If all of them reported to the same Lord, and the Lord asked them to do X, then they included that on the agenda. If that was each chantry needed to provide 5 million dollars in resources by the end of the year to the Lord (to achieve whatever plan he had), then they would do that. That might mean trading some boons. If the other Regents knew that one of them could raise all the cash by themselves, they could just ask him to do it and they owed him one. That way the next time their Lord asked for something he might rely on them to help him achieve whatever. Or if the Lord demanded each chantry control one of the major local media networks, they added that to their agenda and did their best to not have it disrupt what they really wanted to do.<br /> <br /> As long as they could keep their immediate superior happy, each Tremere did their own thing with their remaining free time and resources. And likely thinking how much they'd change things if they ever got to be the one in charge. It was just that everyone knew they needed to &quot;work towards Vienna&quot; - making sure they were contributing to what Vienna wanted done.<br /> <br /> I figure the hallmarks of the Tremere were obedience to the Pyramid and paranoid preparation for conflict with their many enemies. But as long as the chantry was kept adequately prepared and superiors' orders were obeyed, the Tremere could determine their own personal studies or endeavors. The Tremere Oath covers a lot of stuff, but it also allows a lot things too. So Regents usually had a lot of leeway, and the Apprentices that contributed most to his goals were the ones who got promoted most.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T19:40:29-07:00","id":1449502,"title":"","content":"The Tremere have always been one of, if not my most, favorite Clans. The main reason I liked hem wasn\u2019t their magic, it was the pyramid itself. It was the fact that they were a small unpopular Clan who were able to beat the odds through their organization and intelligence. They took vampirism seriously and were able to put aside their own interests enough to work together for the benefit of the Clan and so all Tremere could benefit.<br /> <br /> Magic is cool and all, but I\u2019d rather they lose the magic than their Clan structure if it had to be one or the other.<br /> <br /> For me, what V5 did to the Tremere is the worst part of this edition. Can it be reversed and the Pyramid brought back? Highly unlikely. Maybe it could turn out to be a big plot by the Inner Circle and they are in fact controlling all of the Tremere factions, but I think we all know that isn\u2019t what the designers have in mind and that they\u2019d never do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T00:40:27-07:00","id":1449518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1449484#post1449484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually your issue with the brujah vs. tremere shows exactly what the semi-truck sized plot hole with the Tremere is. Namely what are they when not casting spells. Through out the editions the writers never really explained how the clan paid its bills or maintained influence..</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, no? <br /> <br /> The clan have began life in 1e as the high-flying new money-types. You don't need their financial details to connect the dots. Pin stripped suits, similarities to masonic orders, a clan-first attitude, and that part where they're very direct about being a pyramid scheme? You know Auspex and Dominate are pretty good for money makers right? Even if we assume they're all pure wizards, what about all those retainers they are going to have? Lastly, what the fuck do you actually think they do with all that prestation they get from thaumaturgical services? you think they're only vampire wizards for the sake of being vampire wizards, and every time they cast rituals for a Loaded ventrue they only ask for his occult artefacts and eye of newt monopoly? <br /> <br /> The obvious can't be so elusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T11:51:40-07:00","id":1449572,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t see any reason why the Tremere would have less temporal power than any other Clan, aside from perhaps the Venture who specialize in that. The Tremere have Dominate and the ability to blood bond humans, they are going to have more money and connections than most Clans. Also, the Pyramid provides beneficial connections both in the mortal and vampiric world. For example, if one Tremere has a mortal pawn with a construction company but needs mafia connections to complete a certain project, then another Tremere with organized crime influence would be able to provide aid for a more easily and for a more reasonable fee than some other Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T16:50:33-07:00","id":1449593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1449518#post1449518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh, no?<br /> <br /> The clan have began life in 1e as the high-flying new money-types. You don't need their financial details to connect the dots. Pin stripped suits, similarities to masonic orders, a clan-first attitude, and that part where they're very direct about being a pyramid scheme? You know Auspex and Dominate are pretty good for money makers right? Even if we assume they're all pure wizards, what about all those retainers they are going to have? Lastly, what the fuck do you actually think they do with all that prestation they get from thaumaturgical services? you think they're only vampire wizards for the sake of being vampire wizards, and every time they cast rituals for a Loaded ventrue they only ask for his occult artefacts and eye of newt monopoly?<br /> <br /> The obvious can't be so elusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering we covered this during one of our previous &quot;discussions&quot; I would think you would remember the bullet points. The Tremere rarely make use of ghouls or mortal retainers, please see the Ghouls book on this point. They favored taking care of things themselves and creating specialty minions that didn't leave the chantry except on assignments.<br /> <br /> The Pyramid is a theoretical construct and power structure flow chart for the Tremere, it is not a Pyramid Scheme. The key difference is that pyramid scheme by definition never can contain enough people for everyone involved to turn a profit. The Tremere clan on the other hand wouldn't embrace you unless you had arcane potential (as stated in most Tremere character creation suggestions) and they actually do teach you magic, so they complete the requirements of providing the benefits advertised. This is further bolstered by the fact that the Tremere are a smaller clan since they are so picky about new members and keeping their secrets safe. The pyramid scheme only works if you inflate the clan numbers something rivalling the Brujah or Toreador.<br /> <br /> As for actually writing up where the clan gets their money, I am perfectly happy to infer the use of Auspex and Dominate to gain all sorts of bonuses, especially when combined with that ritual that magically hides a chantry and causes all records of it to self delete, become corrupted, or just get misplaced. But unfortunately there are those players and apparently some V5 writers who apparently require an &quot;information&quot; based bap to the back of the head about what all this stuff actually infers. So yes having it written down for the less creative is a good thing.<br /> <br /> I would also point out that if you are going to bring up where the Tremere were in 1st edition, that would be the only clan with magic. But then feature creep set in and every new clan had their own magics or their own sub-paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T04:32:46-07:00","id":1449641,"title":"","content":"I have the impression that they flip flopped a lot writing the Tremere from book to book (after researching for previous discussions). So depending on what source you look at you can get a significantly different impression.<br /> <br /> For example. My source of choice is -Tremere Revised Chapter Two: Inside the Pyramid. They would absolutely embrace people without magical talent. In fact most apprentices are chosen for other specialities.<br /> <br /> But I am aware that other sources handle it differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T09:47:10-07:00","id":1449669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1449593#post1449593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. The Tremere rarely make use of ghouls or mortal retainers, please see the Ghouls book on this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take a look at literally any other book then. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Tremere clan on the other hand wouldn't embrace you unless you had arcane potential (as stated in most Tremere character creation suggestions) </div> </div> </div>Define &quot;arcane potential&quot;, because that's literally almost everyone. Not having &quot;arcane potential&quot; is a five point flaw for Tremere. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for actually writing up where the clan gets their money, I am perfectly happy to infer the use of Auspex and Dominate to gain all sorts of bonuses, especially when combined with that ritual that magically hides a chantry and causes all records of it to self delete, become corrupted, or just get misplaced. But unfortunately there are those players and apparently some V5 writers who apparently require an &quot;information&quot; based bap to the back of the head about what all this stuff actually infers. So yes having it written down for the less creative is a good thing.<br /> If you need a writeup for how every clan earns it's money and then just assume the ones that don't have suggestions somehow don't make any money at all then only the Ventrue, Setites, Toreador, Ravnos and Assamite Viziers would ever have money. <br /> <br /> I would also point out that if you are going to bring up where the Tremere were in 1st edition, that would be the only clan with magic. But then feature creep set in and every new clan had their own magics or their own sub-paths. </div> </div> </div>I just read up on the 1st edition Tremere. <br /> <br /> Clearly they're meant to be one of the top clans in terms of riches. They see themselves as the second competitiors to the Ventrue They're new money types, their first ever clan picture is a guy in a three piece suit. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V1</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Background: They choose the most aggressive and ambitious people as their Neonates, preferring males. They carefully train and nurture them for years, calling them &quot;apprentices ...<br /> <br /> Character Creation: Tremere usually have a professional and highly educated Con\u00adcept and their Nature and Demeanor tend to be Archetypes connected with power or science. Mental Attributes are primary, as are Knowledge Abilities. They often have the Mentor Background Trait. </div> </div> </div> </div>There are two useful parallels for you in the real world. <br /> First, there's masonic orders or &quot;the Hermetic order of the golden dawn&quot; and the like, where the Tremere take a lot of notes from. Where you can join so long as you've got a job, you're a citizen in good standing, and you've got to believe in, though not necessarily worship, a higher power, meaning you can't be an athiest. <br /> Second is tech companies. Because thaumaturgy rituals are kinda like software; You spend a long time getting it to work initially, but once you've got it, it requires very little to sell your services; there are virtually no parts, there's only labour, and you only need a little labour. Compare that to how the Ventrue gain favours, where they're always losing something to gain something. The Tremere are losing between five and twenty five minutes of their night and little more, gaining huge favours because they're the only people who can do this stuff. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T09:58:30-07:00","id":1449999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1449669#post1449669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take a look at literally any other book then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how late in the development cycle the ghoul book was, I would say it is fairly definitive. Also I have looked at many of the other books, none of them state the concept that you are espousing, so you are still arguing your head canon as far as I am concerned. But if you would like to quote some supplement sources with your point of view, I would happy to look into them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1449669#post1449669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Define &quot;arcane potential&quot;, because that's literally almost everyone. Not having &quot;arcane potential&quot; is a five point flaw for Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>The flaw is a role playing aid for goofy characters or as a story point since merits and flaws, like backgrounds can be gained and lost during play. Did a arcane experiment just fry your ability to cast magic, take the flaw. Was your embrace some sort of arcane ritual that didn't go well, take the flaw. Are you a player who just has to play contradictory characters such as a mage vampire who can't cast magic, take the flaw.<br /> <br /> Also we have discussed the concept in the past that things like hedge magic talents, psychic talents, and other supernatural elements are what the clan are looking for. In other words vampire hogwarts doesn't gift people with the embrace that don't have some inkling of magical talent. In the few cases where some one who can't use magic due to the flaw is embraced, chances are that they have some other magical aspect of worth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1449669#post1449669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just read up on the 1st edition Tremere.<br /> <br /> Clearly they're meant to be one of the top clans in terms of riches. They see themselves as the second competitiors to the Ventrue They're new money types, their first ever clan picture is a guy in a three piece suit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sigh, and once more you can't see the forest for the trees. Any one can steal a three piece suit, so that doesn't mean anything about their wealth, heck Gary from Bloodlines was quite the dresser despite being a sewer rat.<br /> <br /> As for the concept of the Tremere being new money..... nothing could be further from the truth. They were a clan of mages in their mortal days, which means unlimited mortal wealth. The Tremere are the newest clan, but their branch of the mage groups is very old. So you have to keep in mind the difference between how other vampires perceive them and the reality of the Tremere history.<br /> <br /> Vampires might be able to concentrate mortal wealth due to their long life spans and ability to manipulate mortals, but mages can just make things like gold, silver, and gems. So the clan Tremere most likely had quite the pre vampire transition bank balance. Then once they figured out vampire magic and create things like the Path of Conjuring, they still can create out of thin air. A Ventrue could spend kingdoms worth of Resources on a war or endevor until their coffers ran dry, but the Tremere can never go broke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T11:07:08-07:00","id":1450016,"title":"","content":"They were originally described as advisors. Their intended role seemed to be as Jafars: advisors whispering in the Ventrue Sultun's ear and secretly controlling them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T12:36:18-07:00","id":1450039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1449999#post1449999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how late in the development cycle the ghoul book was, I would say it is fairly definitive. Also I have looked at many of the other books, none of them state the concept that you are espousing, so you are still arguing your head canon as far as I am concerned. But if you would like to quote some supplement sources with your point of view, I would happy to look into them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that, but a bunch of the newest V20 books are out-and-out crazy with weird ideas freelancers thought would be cool, like Kiasyd being mixologists or the first power of Quietus allowing assamites to crystalize the hearts of their victims for later consumption. The former is odd, the latter is fucking crazy, perhaps racist, and should never have made it past editing. Being more recent means nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The flaw is a role playing aid for goofy characters or as a story point since merits and flaws, like backgrounds can be gained and lost during play. Did a arcane experiment just fry your ability to cast magic, take the flaw. Was your embrace some sort of arcane ritual that didn't go well, take the flaw. Are you a player who just has to play contradictory characters such as a mage vampire who can't cast magic, take the flaw. </div> </div> </div>Conjecture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also we have discussed the concept in the past that things like hedge magic talents, psychic talents, and other supernatural elements are what the clan are looking for. In other words vampire hogwarts doesn't gift people with the embrace that don't have some inkling of magical talent. In the few cases where some one who can't use magic due to the flaw is embraced, chances are that they have some other magical aspect of worth. </div> </div> </div>Says right here, first edition, they're looking for people from backgrounds of power or science. Business types or science types. Again, real world hermetic types looked for professionals in their social circles. You can learn magic post embrace. Infact looking for mortals who practice magic is counter to what the Tremere are after; achievers, not people who find themselves in fringe groups practicing ideas that probably aren't that hermetic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sigh, and once more you can't see the forest for the trees. Any one can steal a three piece suit, so that doesn't mean anything about their wealth, heck Gary from Bloodlines was quite the dresser despite being a sewer rat. </div> </div> </div>Who can't see what now? Gary is almost certainly loaded.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the concept of the Tremere being new money..... nothing could be further from the truth. They were a clan of mages in their mortal days, which means unlimited mortal wealth. The Tremere are the newest clan, but their branch of the mage groups is very old. So you have to keep in mind the difference between how other vampires perceive them and the reality of the Tremere history. </div> </div> </div>New money, do you know what that actually means? It's not how long you've had your money for, it's your attitude, your lifestyle, your social circle, the way you work with friends, how likely you are to take risks. The Tremere are very much new money, and they want new-money types in the clan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . So the clan Tremere most likely had quite the pre vampire transition bank balance. Then once they figured out vampire magic and create things like the Path of Conjuring, they still can create out of thin air. A Ventrue could spend kingdoms worth of Resources on a war or endevor until their coffers ran dry, but the Tremere can never go broke. </div> </div> </div>1- you can't melt down the gold you conjure, let's not get into price fluctuations from it becoming commonly available.<br /> 2- They made their money through connections and services only they offer. They continue to make money with connections and services only they offer. Simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T14:27:20-07:00","id":1450734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houston810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1449362#post1449362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there one written out for V20?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, it was copy/paste'd in Rites of the Blood<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T16:23:56-07:00","id":1450745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1450734#post1450734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, it was copy/paste'd in Rites of the Blood<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you good Sir","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T10:54:40-07:00","id":1456080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1449331#post1449331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC in V5 there isn't a &quot;Transubstantiation of Seven&quot; ritual translation yet for the Tremere, and with the Council gone (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere Council of Seven is not necessarily gone! Come on, they are such rich and interesting characters; and while few players probably used the Inner Councilors in their games, their wide-reaching influence on the whole Clan Tremere was constantly referred to in the setting descriptions, including both Tremere Clan Books.<br /> It just doesn't make sense, that a group of seven 4th Generation (Or 5th? Was it ever confirmed that they all lowered their Generation to 4th?) Vampires could have been blindsided by an attack as simple and brute as launching missiles at them.<br /> They all have access to Auspex and Thaumaturgy of 6th-9th levels.With Auspex comes precognition and the ability to divine information, and also to scry at distant locations. Thaumaturgy can also offer these, and also direct protection and misdirection. As far as I see it - yes, some missiles were launched in Vienna, but they just hit some random buildings.<br /> <br /> As to why the Inner Councilors would allow this - well, maybe they wanted to see the reaction of Tremere Vampires, and other Vampires also, at their seeming demise. Or maybe they wanted to prop up and galvanize Karl Shrekt. Or to do a general reshuffling of Clan Tremere. The overall Blood Bond to the Councilors faded because they did a grand ritual that resulted in this - they deemed that Tremere Vampires no longer need such enforcement of loyalty.<br /> <br /> If this doesn't convince you, consider this - how could such a striking and fearsome Thaumaturgist as Elaine the Calinot be defeated by mere mortals? Or by Vampires, for that matter.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <a href=\"http://gravidja.free.fr/arborescence/bynight/le_caire/picsqahira/helene.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://gravidja.free.fr/arborescence...ira/helene.jpg</a> (I dunno why the picture is labeled Helene)<br /> <img src=\"http://gravidja.free.fr/arborescence/bynight/le_caire/picsqahira/helene.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> If this illustration does not convince you, how about another Inner Councilor - Thomas Wyncham?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/f/f9/TW.png/revision/latest?cb=20160104175543\" target=\"_blank\">https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/wh...20160104175543</a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Now the Inner Councilors coming back to the fore would be a major change. But House Goratrix reemerging in V5 sets precedence. Or actually - the precedence for Tremere Vampires coming back from seeming demise was set long ago, by Malgorzata, a Childe of Goratrix. In VtM books she suffered a horrible fate at the hands of early anarchs. But in the card game Vampire: the Eternal Struggle, she is back, as the most awesome Priscus. (Note that Malgorzata is on Road of Sin, Path of the Devil - rating 6, at least - so her attire is entirely appropriate.)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/3/3e/Malgorzata_VTES.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20140620022322\" target=\"_blank\">https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/wh...20140620022322</a> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-03-2021, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T17:51:21-07:00","id":1456095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just doesn't make sense, that a group of seven 4th Generation (Or 5th? Was it ever confirmed that they all lowered their Generation to 4th?) Vampires could have been blindsided by an attack as simple and brute as launching missiles at them</div> </div> </div> </div>Why, might you ask? You're exactly right on everything you say.. but the true simple answer as to the why, in the case of these very low gen Tremere being done-in by a simple airstrike (despite their numerous Disciplines, especially Auspex, as you rightfully posit); is that it's just a case of a V5ism. <br /> <br /> I doubt we will be seeing the V5 Council come to form at all. This edition, they seem to be in the cuffs of trying to erase this Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T00:41:15-07:00","id":1456107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1449999#post1449999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also we have discussed the concept in the past that things like hedge magic talents, psychic talents, and other supernatural elements are what the clan are looking for. In other words vampire hogwarts doesn't gift people with the embrace that don't have some inkling of magical talent. In the few cases where some one who can't use magic due to the flaw is embraced, chances are that they have some other magical aspect of worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be how you to prefer to conceive of the clan, but it's not how the Tremere have been portrayed in published books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Abraham DuSable was a lawyer.<br /> <br /> Victor was a CIA agent.<br /> <br /> Helena Tayor was an Awakened mage.<br /> <br /> Martin Franckel was an engineering student.<br /> <br /> Wan Zhu was a museum curator.<br /> <br /> Masika St. John was a computer science professor.<br /> <br /> Garwood Marshall was a jazz musician.<br /> <br /> Marie D'Richet was either an Awakened mage or being groomed to Awaken by her mage father.<br /> <br /> Hyapatia was an archaeology student.<br /> <br /> Valois Sang was a psychiatrist.<br /> <br /> Carna was a peasant girl.<br /> <br /> The Revised clanbook sample PCs had a coyote, a medical examiner, a nightclub owner, a corporate middle manager, a directionless smart kid, a union leader, an aspiring politician, and a security consultant. </div> </div> </div>We can see here that the Tremere by no means limit themselves to prospective childer who are already well-versed in the occult. The clan favors intellectual types, people who function well in a hierarchy, and preferably both. There are also exceptions like Garwood Marshall and Carna who don't neatly fit either of those molds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T01:16:48-07:00","id":1456109,"title":"","content":"I think the Tremere of earlier eras were very much products of the original House Tremere and embraced exclusively or predominantly people who had occult powers, hermetic training, or some other proven aptitude for &quot;magic.&quot; They were still getting use to being vampires, still had a lot of mortal members in the House, and wanted the same kind of people. You were recruited first to House Tremere and then embraced afterwards. Old habits died hard.<br /> <br /> But the modern era Tremere were clearly looking at other kinds of people who nevertheless displayed a lot of ambition and natural talents who would fit well in the Pyramid. Magic was increasingly a secondary consideration. It wasn't that they weren't embracing those anymore. They still did. It's just they wanted <i>other</i> kinds of people that could help the clan in the modern world.<br /> <br /> At the same time, there were always people who were embraced simply because certain influential Tremere, who had enough pull that they were allowed to create childer, wanted certain people as their childe. And this is where we see a lot of character concepts that don't fit in all eras.<br /> <br /> 1e Chicago By Night is a good example of this trend. The leader was Nicolai, someone who was an apprentice living mage who became embraced after his sire was turned into a vampire. But he embraced Abraham DuSable not for his magical talents, but because he was very useful in other ways for the Chicago chantry. It just happened that DuSable thrived in learning Thaumaturgy. DuSable did well enough to get permission to sire, but settled on the musician Garwood who was essentially a passion embrace and didn't work out. (His other childe, the caitiff Maldavis was very similar). The other childe of Nicolai, Tracy Graves, was essentially of the earlier tradition and embraced because of her occult interest (combined with Nicolai's obsession with her).<br /> <br /> In Milwaukee By Night, Carna was clearly a passion embrace that didn't make sense, but the Clan retroactively approved it. Her sire Bourdona was clearly influential enough in the clan (and he was a Prince somewhere) that it was tolerated. A different Tremere doing the same thing might have gotten severely punished at the time. (Carna's embrace date of 1435 was in the middle of the Anarch Revolt; they might have needed Bourdona a lot at the time, or thought retro-approving Carna was a good PR move). But Carna clearly took to Thaumaturgy so it worked out. Dr Mortius was a mortal practitioner of the occult, and that is why he was embraced in an older age. But Victor, the CIA assassin, was clearly embraced for other reasons.<br /> <br /> I would say that very early on the Clan only embraced people who would have fit in the old House Tremere. However, as time went by and the world changed, the clan slowly opened up their selection criteria as they identified other required skills the Clan needed to survive and grow in power. Over time this probably changed from something like 90% occult and 10% other, to something now that might be more like 20% occult background and 80% other. Those last figures can obviously be fiddled with - I haven't done any analysis to get them, it's just something I threw out there. But I would say at most it's likely 50/50 in terms of occult.<br /> <br /> They probably still want people who seem to have an aptitude for hermetic magic. They want people who could theoretically devote themselves and improve. But it's no longer the primary consideration. Likely any chantry wants some members who have the interest and talent to excel in thaumaturgy. And if a chantry currently doesn't have such an Apprentice, they would prioritize that. But after they have one or two members who can do that, then they might prioritize other kind of members that they need. Perhaps even someone who doesn't fit at all, but whom they needed for a very specific reason.<br /> <br /> And of course, embraces that end up being a big mistake can happen at any time for any place, because even Tremere become irrational or make mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T03:34:03-07:00","id":1456115,"title":"","content":"Since I've been trying to synthethize the v5 fluff into something more consistant with previous lore, I've made it clear that the Tremere are currently re-establishing the pyramid since going solo is a death sentance with 4 clans, 1 bloodline, the order of hermes the 2nd inquisition and frankly any mystic who wants your books out to get their pound of flesh. I figure at least one of the 7 survived (probably Etrius).<br /> I've also made house Carna more sinister &quot;burn people alive in a wicker man&quot; or the &quot;If Tremere had been a Verbanna&quot; Pagans with links with lileth cultists and possibly Kupula. Plus they're organized deliberatly as a circle rather than a pyramid. I figure they're currently weighing their options with weither to cut a deal with the Pyramid or go anarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}